{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "spread_gated_cluster_boost",
  "intent": "Augment parent with a spread-gated cluster_density term that activates only when candidate-to-unvisited spread is low (uniform-like instances where regret is statistically noisy). Keeps parent's quadratic return-distance ramp and spread-reliability regret gating intact, preserving strong clustered/grid behavior. Hypothesis: in uniform instances, local density (fraction of nearby unvisited cities) is a more reliable structural proxy than regret when all candidates appear equidistant, helping break ties and reduce the parent's residual uniform gap. Bounded weight (max ~0.12) and gated by (1-rel) ensures it acts as a tiebreaker, never overriding distance dominance or perturbing high-spread regimes.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "nonlinear"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    p = f['progress']\n    s = f['spread']\n    rel = s / (0.4 + s + 1e-9)\n    rw = 0.15 + 0.4 * p + 0.3 * p * p\n    rgw = (0.05 + 0.15 * p) * (0.3 + 0.7 * rel)\n    cdw = 0.12 * (1.0 - rel)\n    return -f['distance'] + rw * f['return_distance'] + rgw * f['regret'] + 0.05 * f['nearest_remaining'] + cdw * f['cluster_density']",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 17,
  "reference_id": null,
